The discussion focused on developing an OpenAI-based GPT system in Python to function as an agent with long-term memory. Key points included structuring the memory system using `LongTermMemory` and `ConversationMemory` to handle memory across conversations and provide selective memory recalls. Best practices for memory types were established, emphasizing the importance of session and episodic memories and retrieval structures. Prototypes for classes and functions were outlined, including `MemoryRow`, `TaskRow`, and their respective storage implementations using SQLAlchemy and Whoosh. Additionally, unit tests were proposed to ensure the functionality of the conversation and long-term memory systems, with a focus on retaining memory isolation between multiple users. The conversation concluded with a roadmap for the implementation of mock models and pytest files to thoroughly evaluate the system.
